* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
* CREATE.ACCOUNT USER  <name> {ADMINISTRATOR | PROGRAMMER} {SH-ON} {OS-ON} {NO.QUERY}
* CREATE.ACCOUNT GROUP <name> {ADMINISTRATOR | PROGRAMMER} {NO.QUERY}
* CREATE.ACCOUNT OTHER <name> <pathname> {ADMINISTRATOR | PROGRAMMER} {NO.QUERY}
*
* SH-ON and OS-ON (10 Sep 26, the port's) grant a USER account the SH verb's
* shell and OS.EXECUTE; they are accepted on any type and recorded only for a
* USER account below ADMINISTRATOR, as the port's grant.os.access.
*
* 09 Sep 26 dm - THIS BLOCK WAS STALE AND IT COST SOMETHING, WHICH IS WHY IT IS
*   CORRECTED RATHER THAN JUST EXTENDED.  It read
*   "CREATE.ACCOUNT account.name path.name [NO.QUERY]", the pre-0.9.0 form:
*   USER/GROUP/OTHER has been required since rev 0.9.0 and only OTHER takes a
*   pathname.  A session writing message 10033 copied this line, shipped
*   "CREATE.ACCOUNT name path ADMINISTRATOR" as advice to an administrator, and
*   the owner caught it - the command would have failed if typed.  ***THE
*   SYNTAX THE VERB PRINTS AT :246 IS THE TRUTH; THIS BLOCK IS COMMENTARY AND
*   HAD DRIFTED.***  The port's copy of this same block is stale in the same
*   way - do not take it from there either.
*
*   NOTE THE PORT HAS A KEYWORD THIS TREE DOES NOT: its documented grammar is
*   "create.account user <name> {administrator | programmer}
*   <ssh | api | both | none> {no.query}", with the remote-access keyword
*   REQUIRED for a user account.  That is PRE_RELEASE 13's work and is not
*   built here, so it is absent rather than optional - a conformity gap, named
*   so it is not mistaken for a difference of opinion.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
